Selected state-Stein source closure from Physlib:
https://github.com/leanprover-community/physlib
Revision: f6e446ca99fd83b3a60743a61900cb2acb98f531.
Original author/copyright headers are retained. The upstream project is
Apache-2.0; its license is reproduced in LICENSE.

The supplied compatibility port originally contained 68 upstream modules
and seven state-Stein bridge modules. This release retains the 60 upstream
modules and all seven bridges required by the generalized-channel project.
Unused sources, historical audit material and port logs are omitted.

Compatibility target: Lean 4.29.0-rc6 and mathlib
f156f7abd91ac67adb22bf999e5a71ba22e22e41.
The original port record names Lean 4.34.1 and mathlib
d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612 as its source-audit versions.
Proof adaptations include import relocations, API/structure/coercion
changes and explicit finite-dimensional matrix proof steps. Retained
proof sources are unchanged by the present release cleanup.

Overlapping trace-inequality modules re-export the shared Quantum
implementation. Sion minimax has one canonical implementation under
QuantumInfo/ForMathlib; the channel library re-exports it.

The seven bridge modules are SingletonTheory, SingletonSteinBridge,
TupleCoherence, TupleStates, OrdinaryStateStein, KernelFilledAlternative,
and StateSteinDirect. They establish singleton state-Stein results,
tensor coherence, singular-support reduction, and eventual tests in
natural and base-two units.

upstream-source-sha256.txt retains the original upstream hash inventory;
source-sha256.txt records the distributed subset. No source outside this
subset is included. Reuse does not imply endorsement by source authors.
